---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { config } from "../../config";
---
<Legal title="Guarantee & warranty" description="Your legal rights if an olácompanion is faulty: your UK statutory rights.">
  <p>
    Your legal rights come first. Nothing on this page limits them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your statutory rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the Consumer Rights Act 2015, the watch must be of satisfactory quality, fit for purpose and as described.
    If it isn't:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>within 30 days of delivery you can reject it for a full refund;</li>
    <li>within 6 months, we will repair or replace it; if that fails, you are entitled to a refund or price reduction;</li>
    <li>you can claim for up to 6 years (5 years in Scotland), although after 6 months you may need to show the fault was there at delivery.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to make a claim</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${config.supportEmail}`}>{config.supportEmail}</a> with your order number and a short
    description of the problem. We cover the cost of returning a faulty watch.
  </p>

  <h2>Commercial warranty</h2>
  <p>
    We do not currently offer an additional commercial warranty beyond your legal rights.
  </p>

  <h2>What isn't covered by legal rights</h2>
  <p>Normal wear and tear, accidental damage, and damage from misuse or unauthorised repair.</p>
</Legal>
